---
import HistoryIntroduction from './HistoryIntroduction.astro';
import ComparisonBars from './ComparisonBars.astro';
import HistoryTimeline from './HistoryTimeline.astro';
import HistoryMap from './HistoryMap.astro';
import HistoryEvidence from './HistoryEvidence.astro';
import HistoryDetails from './HistoryDetails.astro';
import {dates,year,href} from '../../scripts/static/history-page.mjs';
import {ordinal} from '../domain/timeline';
import {temporalLabel} from '../domain/history-queries';
import {outsideVisiblePeriod} from '../domain/comparison';
import HistoryRegionalEvidence from './HistoryRegionalEvidence.astro';
import type {HistoryPage} from '../presentation/history-page';
interface Props {page: HistoryPage}
const {page}=Astro.props;
const {state}=page;
---
<header><a href="./" class="brand">historica <span>▥</span></a><span class="beta-sash" title="Beta: features and historical coverage are still developing">BETA</span><span class="brand-tagline">Visualising history</span><a href="/about" class="about-link">About</a><button id="share">Copy this view</button></header><main><noscript><p>The default timeline, places and sources are shown below. Enable JavaScript to adjust dates, search and move the map.</p><nav aria-label="Connected histories">{page.related.map(e=><p><a href={href(e)}>{e.title}</a></p>)}</nav></noscript><p id="error" role="alert" hidden></p><section class="collection-search" aria-label="Search history"><label class="sr-only" for="history-search">Search history</label><div class="search-input-row"><input id="history-search" type="search" placeholder="Search a person, place or event…" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="search-help" aria-controls="search-results"><button id="search-clear" type="button" hidden>Clear search</button></div><p id="search-help" class="sr-only">Find people, places, periods and events across the whole collection.</p><div id="search-panel" hidden><p id="search-count" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><ul id="search-results"></ul></div></section>
<HistoryIntroduction page={page} /><section class="opening-comparison" aria-labelledby="comparison-title"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="comparison-title">At the same time</h2><span id="comparison-range">{dates(state.start,state.end)}</span></div><p id="comparison-intro">{page.explanation}</p><details class="people-comparison"><summary>Compare two people</summary><div class="people-selectors"><label>First person <select id="compare-first"><option value="">Choose a person</option></select></label><label>Second person <select id="compare-second"><option value="">Choose a person</option></select></label><button id="compare-reset">Use suggestions</button></div><p>Choose any two lives. Their full ranges are shown, including when they did not overlap.</p></details><ComparisonBars page={page} /><div class="comparison-modes" role="group" aria-label="Comparison scale"><button id="comparison-shared" aria-pressed="true">Shared years</button><button id="comparison-full" aria-pressed="false">Full date ranges</button></div><button class="full-timeline-link" id="jump-timeline">Explore the full timeline ↓</button></section><details class="suggested-journeys" open><summary>Start with a question</summary><div class="journey-links"><button data-focus="stonehenge">What was happening elsewhere while Stonehenge was being built?</button><button data-focus="julius-caesar" data-kind="person">Who was alive at the same time as Julius Caesar?</button><button data-focus="socrates">How did Socrates’ life overlap the Peloponnesian War?</button></div></details><div class="timeline-map-layout"><section class="graphical-timeline" aria-labelledby="swim-heading"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="swim-heading">The wider timeline</h2><span id="swim-count">{page.ranked.length} of {page.ranked.length} matching entries</span></div><details class="timeline-options"><summary id="options-summary">Adjust dates and filters</summary><div class="date-display"><h2 id="range-title">{dates(state.start,state.end)}</h2><div class="controls"><button id="zoom-out">− Wider</button><button id="fit">{page.focus.type==='person'?'Full lifespan':'Fit study period'}</button><button id="zoom-in">+ Closer</button></div></div><section class="window-controls" aria-label="Visible time window"><label>From <output id="start-label">{year(state.start)}</output><input id="start" type="range" min={ordinal(state.start)} max={ordinal(state.end)} value={ordinal(state.start)} aria-valuetext={year(state.start)} aria-label="Start of visible period"></label><label>To <output id="end-label">{year(state.end)}</output><input id="end" type="range" min={ordinal(state.start)} max={ordinal(state.end)} value={ordinal(state.end)} aria-valuetext={year(state.end)} aria-label="End of visible period"></label></section>
<div class="filters"><label>Show <select id="kind"><option value="all">All context</option><option value="event">Events</option><option value="period">Periods</option><option value="person">People</option></select></label><label>Near <select id="area"><option value="all">Everywhere</option><option value="egypt">Egypt</option><option value="macedonia">Macedonia</option><option value="bactria">Bactria</option></select></label><button id="clear">Clear filters</button></div></details><div class="year-explorer"><label><input type="checkbox" id="year-enabled"> Explore a single year</label><div id="year-controls" hidden><div class="year-heading"><button id="year-prev" aria-label="Previous year">←</button><output id="year-label" for="year-cursor"></output><button id="year-next" aria-label="Next year">→</button></div><input id="year-cursor" type="range" aria-label="Year to explore"><p>The timeline keeps its full window. The map shows dated associations for this year.</p><details><summary id="living-count">People alive in this year</summary><p>Based on recorded lifespans; ages are year-level estimates. Approximate dates remain approximate.</p><div id="living-people"></div></details></div></div><p class="swim-key"><span>━ Lives</span><span>▬ Periods</span><span>◆ Events</span> · Select an entry to explore it. Arrows continue beyond the window. <span class="date-key">Hatched bars: approximate dates or context windows, not continuous activity.</span></p><div class="swim-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Graphical timeline. Scroll horizontally to explore dates; regional labels stay visible."><HistoryTimeline page={page} /></div><p class="muted footnote">Select any entry to change focus. Lanes group recorded places, not exact journeys. Swipe sideways on smaller screens.</p></section><aside class="geography"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="map-title">{page.regionPaths.length?page.focus.title:'Related places'}</h2><span id="map-count">{page.places.length} dated associations</span></div><div class="controls map-controls"><button id="map-in" aria-label="Zoom map in">+</button><button id="map-out" aria-label="Zoom map out">−</button><button id="map-world">World</button><button id="map-fit" disabled={!page.places.length&&!page.regionPaths.length}>{page.regionPaths.length?'Fit area':'Related places'}</button></div><label class="border-control">Modern borders <input id="map-borders" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.05" value="1"></label><HistoryMap page={page} /><p class="map-key">Drag or two-finger scroll to pan · pinch or +/− to zoom · select a gold marker to change focus. Green land or ring: focus area. Gold circles: approximate associated areas. Modern borders provide orientation. Circles are not territory boundaries.</p><div id="map-places">{page.places.map(a=>{const target=page.data.entities.find(e=>e.id===a.place);return <div class="place-row"><span><strong>{a.label}</strong><small>{dates(a.startYear,a.endYear)}{temporalLabel(a,state)?` · ${temporalLabel(a,state)}`:''}</small></span>{target&&target.id!==state.focus&&<button data-focus={target.id}>Focus on {target.title}</button>}</div>})}</div><p id="map-empty" class="muted">{page.regionPaths.length?'Green shows Britain and Ireland using today’s land outline for orientation, not ancient borders. Gold markers show dated records in the selected period.':page.places.length?'Only associations overlapping the visible period are highlighted.':'No dated place associations recorded for this focus in this period. This is a gap in the sample.'}</p><details><summary>Evidence and map credits</summary><HistoryEvidence page={page} /><p>Base geography: <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/">Natural Earth</a>, public domain. Bactria’s dashed southern heartland is an editorial sketch, not a political frontier.</p></details></aside></div><details class="connections-panel"><summary>People and places connected to this focus</summary><section class="related"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Connected to this focus</h2><span>Choose a new focus, or narrow the context with a filter.</span></div><div id="related">{page.related.map(e=><div class="related-item"><button data-focus={e.id}><small>{e.type}</small><strong>{e.title}</strong><span>{e.relation}</span>{outsideVisiblePeriod(e)&&<span class="outside-window">Outside visible period</span>}</button>{['area','state','city'].includes(e.type)&&<button class="filter-link" data-filter={e.id}>Filter near {e.title}</button>}</div>)}</div></section>
</details><details class="browse-panel"><summary>More ways to explore</summary><nav class="navigation"><button id="back" disabled>Back to previous focus</button><label>Explore <select id="focus-picker" aria-label="Choose a focus"></select></label><span id="focus-count">ONE FOCUS · CONNECTED HISTORIES</span></nav>
<section class="world-browse" aria-label="Explore the collection"><button id="whole-period">Ancient world · 3000 BCE–200 CE</button><button data-focus="world-400-250">The world · 400–250 BCE</button><button data-focus="britain-ireland">Britain and Ireland</button><button data-focus="athens">Athens</button><button data-focus="persia">Persia</button><button data-focus="china">China</button><button data-focus="india">South Asia</button><button data-focus="rome">Rome</button><button data-focus="oaxaca">Oaxaca</button></section></details><div class="workspace"><section class="timeline"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Explore the details</h2></div><div class="axis"><span>RELATION / DISTANCE</span><div id="ticks"><span>{year(state.start)}</span><span>{year(state.end)}</span></div></div><p class="muted" id="context-count">{page.ranked.length} matching lives, events and periods</p><HistoryDetails page={page} /><button id="more-context" hidden={page.ranked.length<=18}>Show all {page.ranked.length} items</button><p class="muted footnote">Nearest context sits closest to the focus. Distances use overlapping dated associations and approximate reference points; they are not exact personal locations. “Location not researched” means that the collection lacks a dated location for this comparison. Regional membership is used where recorded; other area filters use an approximate 1,200 km vicinity, not historical borders.</p></section>
</div>
<HistoryRegionalEvidence page={page} /><footer><p><a href="/">Home</a> · <a href="/about">About Historica</a></p><p>Beta · Sources and dates are still being checked. <a href="coverage.html">What you can trust, and what’s missing</a>.</p>Selected ancient histories · 3000 BCE–200 CE, with earlier predynastic and later context. Coverage remains uneven. Missing records mean gaps in coverage, not an absence of history. <a href="coverage.html">Research coverage</a> · <a href="campaign.html">Earlier campaign prototype</a><p>Historica is an open source site on <a href="https://github.com/sproates/historica">GitHub</a>.</p></footer><div id="status" role="status" class="sr-only"></div></main>
